{
  "$schema": "../schema/stage-demo.schema.json",
  "id": "stage-demo",
  "type": "stage-demo",
  "status": "DEMO — not final casting",
  "purpose": "Four worked theatre-of-the-mind scenes, built to see what design/theatre-of-the-mind-staging.md actually looks like with real art in a real Foundry world. Each scene demonstrates one staging arrangement.",
  "notes": [
    "The portrait assignments below are a DEMO CAST, not a decision. Deciding which face belongs to which character is the job of the already-accepted asset-review-pipeline idea (AI-catalogued, human-confirmed, organised out of artwork/in-tray/), and it is explicitly the user's creative call — see CLAUDE.md's rule about not finalising the six kids. Nothing here writes back to data/characters/ or data/npcs/.",
    "Sources are filenames inside artwork/in-tray/, which is gitignored and large. tools/stage-assets/stage_assets.py reads this file, resizes each source, and writes the result into the module's own assets/stage/ directory under the stable id given here. The id is the contract; the source filename is expected to change when the real pipeline organises the in-tray.",
    "The three Directorate NPCs genuinely have no names yet (data/npcs/*.json carry null names and role titles only), so their role titles are used verbatim rather than invented around. `bar-regular` is a deliberately unaffiliated civilian (faction: null) added alongside them so the Splash tier's monochrome default and its Directorate-red accent both have a real demo case in one scene (stage-demo-bar)."
  ],
